==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From Old Norse {{term|Old Norse|súrr|lang=is}}, which came from {{proto|Germanic|suraz|lang=is}}, .
===Adjective===
'''súr''' {{m|f}}, [[súrt]] {{n}}

# [[sour]], [[tart]], [[acid]]
# (of mood) [[surly]], [[bitter]], [[morose]], [[sour]]
#: ''Ekki vera svona '''súr'''.''
#:: Don't be so '''morose'''.

